/-!
# The super Shapovalov pairing on the free algebra

Let `A` be a symmetrizable generalized Cartan matrix with a super-admissible parity `τ`, `P` a
realization of `A` over a field `K` of characteristic zero and `Λ` a weight with
`⟨Λ, αᵢ^∨⟩ = nᵢ ∈ ℕ`, `nᵢ` even for odd `τᵢ`. Write `y ↦ f(y) v̄_Λ` for the map
`T(V) = K⟨vᵢ⟩ → M̄(Λ)`, `vᵢ ↦ fᵢ`.

The relation `eᵢ fⱼ = (-1)^{τᵢτⱼ} fⱼ eᵢ + δᵢⱼ αᵢ^∨` shows that `eᵢ` acts on `f(y) v̄_Λ` through
the twisted Verma-type operator `Eᵢ = LusztigF.twistVermaOp i sᵢ cᵢ` with signs
`sᵢ(j) = (-1)^{τᵢτⱼ}` and coefficients `cᵢ(μ) = nᵢ - ⟨μ, αᵢ^∨⟩`:
`eᵢ (f(y) v̄_Λ) = f(Eᵢ y) v̄_Λ` (`GVerma.e_smul_fAlg_smul_hwv`). The resulting pairing
`S(w, y) = ε(E_w y)` (`LusztigF.twistVermaForm`) is the super analogue of the classical Shapovalov
pairing `LusztigF.vermaForm`.

**Theorem** (`mem_superSerreIdeal_of_twistVermaForm_eq_zero`). If `y` has weight `ν` with
`νᵢ ≤ nᵢ` for all `i`, and `S(w, y) = 0` for all words `w` of weight `ν`, then `y` lies in the
ideal `(sᵢⱼ)` of `T(V)` generated by the super Serre elements.

Proof: the conditions say that all products of the `eᵢ` of weight `ν` kill the image of
`f(y) v̄_Λ` in `L̃(Λ) = M̄(Λ) / ∑ᵢ U fᵢ^{nᵢ+1} v̄_Λ`. By induction on `ν`, this image is killed by
every `eᵢ`; a nonzero such vector of weight `Λ - ν`, `ν ≠ 0`, would generate a proper submodule
of the irreducible module `L̃(Λ)` ([Kac78] Thm. 2 (c), `GVerma.isSimpleModule_fPowQuotient`).
So `f(y) v̄_Λ ∈ ∑ᵢ U fᵢ^{nᵢ+1} v̄_Λ`, whose weights are below some `Λ - (nᵢ + 1) αᵢ`; since
`νᵢ < nᵢ + 1`, `f(y) v̄_Λ = 0`, i.e. `y ∈ (sᵢⱼ)`
(`GVerma.fAlg_smul_hwv_eq_zero_iff_mem_superSerreIdeal`).
This replaces the nondegeneracy of a contravariant form, which is not formalized for `G(A, τ)`.
The argument is our own.

## Main definitions

* `Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping.superVermaCoeff`: the coefficients `cᵢ(μ) = nᵢ - ⟨μ, αᵢ^∨⟩`.
* `Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping.superSerreFamily`: the super Serre elements as a family
  indexed by the pairs `i ≠ j`, of weights `superSerreWeight`.

## Main results

* `Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping.GVerma.e_smul_fAlg_smul_hwv`: `eᵢ f(y) v̄_Λ = f(Eᵢ y) v̄_Λ`.
* `Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping.GVerma.mem_superSerreIdeal_of_twistVermaForm_eq_zero`: the
  kernel of the super Shapovalov pairing in weights `ν ≤ n` is contained in `(sᵢⱼ)`.
* `LusztigF.exists_twistVermaForm_eq_mul`: for signs `sᵢⱼ² = 1`, the twisted pairing is a unit
  multiple of the untwisted pairing `LusztigF.vermaForm` with coefficients multiplied by the sign
  characters `μ ↦ ∏ⱼ sᵢⱼ^{μⱼ}`.
* `LusztigF.mem_superSerreIdeal_of_shapovalovMap_eq_zero`: the same kernel statement for a Lusztig
  Cartan datum and the untwisted pairing, in the form used by quantum dimension counts (the super
  analogue of `LusztigF.mem_serreSpan_of_shapovalovMap_eq_zero`).
* `Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping.mem_superSerreIdeal_iff_mem_productSpan`: the weight-`ν`
  part of `(sᵢⱼ)` is spanned by the products `a sᵢⱼ b` of weight `ν` with words `a`, `b`.

## References

* [Kac78] V. G. Kac, *Infinite-dimensional algebras, Dedekind's η-function, classical Möbius
  function and the very strange formula*, Adv. Math. **30** (1978), 85–136, §1.2, Thm. 2.
-/

open Module FreeAlgebra LusztigF

noncomputable section

namespace LusztigF

variable {R X : Type*} [Field R] [DecidableEq X]

/-! ### Comparison with untwisted operators

For signs `sⱼ` with `sⱼ² = 1`, the twisted operator is an untwisted one up to a sign on each
weight space: with the character `χ(μ) = ∏ⱼ sⱼ^{μⱼ}`,
`twistVermaOp i s c y = χ(μ) sᵢ • vermaOp i (χ c) y` for `y` of weight `μ`. -/

omit [DecidableEq X] in
lemma weightSign_mul_self (s : X → R) (hs : ∀ j, s j * s j = 1) (μ : X →₀ ℕ) :
    weightSign s μ * weightSign s μ = 1 := by
  rw [weightSign, ← Finsupp.prod_mul]
  exact Finset.prod_eq_one fun j _ ↦ by
    change s j ^ μ j * s j ^ μ j = 1
    rw [← mul_pow, hs, one_pow]

theorem twistVermaOp_wordBasis_eq (i : X) (s : X → R) (hs : ∀ j, s j * s j = 1)
    (c : (X →₀ ℕ) → R) (w : List X) :
    twistVermaOp i s c (wordBasis R X w) =
      (weightSign s (wordWeight w) * s i) •
        vermaOp i (fun μ ↦ weightSign s μ * c μ) (wordBasis R X w) := by
  induction w with
  | nil => simp
  | cons j w ih =>
    rw [← ι_mul_wordBasis, twistVermaOp_ι_mul, ih, vermaOp_ι_mul, weightScale_wordBasis,
      weightScale_wordBasis, wordWeight_cons, weightSign_add, weightSign_single, pow_one, smul_add,
      mul_smul_comm, smul_smul]
    congr 1
    · congr 1; ring
    · split_ifs with hij
      · subst hij
        rw [smul_smul]
        congr 1
        linear_combination (-c (wordWeight w) * weightSign s (wordWeight w) *
          weightSign s (wordWeight w)) * hs i - c (wordWeight w) *
          weightSign_mul_self s hs (wordWeight w)
      · simp

theorem twistVermaOp_eq_smul (i : X) (s : X → R) (hs : ∀ j, s j * s j = 1)
    (c : (X →₀ ℕ) → R) {μ : X →₀ ℕ} {y : FreeAlgebra R X} (hy : y ∈ wordSpan R μ) :
    twistVermaOp i s c y =
      (weightSign s μ * s i) • vermaOp i (fun ν ↦ weightSign s ν * c ν) y := by
  induction hy using wordSpan_induction with
  | word w hw => rw [twistVermaOp_wordBasis_eq i s hs, hw]
  | zero => simp
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => rw [map_add, map_add, hy, hz, smul_add]
  | smul a y _ hy => rw [map_smul, map_smul, hy, smul_comm]

/-- For involutive signs, the twisted pairing of `w` with `y` of weight `μ` is a unit multiple of
the untwisted pairing with the coefficients `cᵢ(ν)` multiplied by `χᵢ(ν) = ∏ⱼ sᵢⱼ^{νⱼ}`. -/
theorem exists_twistVermaForm_eq_mul (s : X → X → R) (hs : ∀ i j, s i j * s i j = 1)
    (c : X → (X →₀ ℕ) → R) (w : List X) (μ : X →₀ ℕ) :
    ∃ u : R, u * u = 1 ∧ ∀ y ∈ wordSpan R μ, twistVermaForm s c w y =
      u * vermaForm (fun i ν ↦ weightSign (s i) ν * c i ν) w y := by
  induction w generalizing μ with
  | nil => exact ⟨1, by simp, fun y _ ↦ by simp [twistVermaForm_apply, vermaForm_apply]⟩
  | cons i w ih =>
    obtain ⟨u, hu, h⟩ := ih (μ - Finsupp.single i 1)
    refine ⟨u * (weightSign (s i) μ * s i i), ?_, fun y hy ↦ ?_⟩
    · linear_combination (weightSign (s i) μ * s i i) ^ 2 * hu +
        s i i * s i i * weightSign_mul_self (s i) (hs i) μ + hs i i
    · rw [twistVermaForm_cons, twistVermaOp_eq_smul i (s i) (hs i) (c i) hy, map_smul,
        h _ (vermaOp_mem_wordSpan i _ hy), vermaForm_cons, smul_eq_mul]
      ring

theorem vermaOp_mul_coeff (i : X) (c : (X →₀ ℕ) → R) (κ : R) :
    vermaOp i (fun μ ↦ κ * c μ) = κ • vermaOp i c := by
  rw [← twistVermaOp_one_sign, ← twistVermaOp_one_sign, twistVermaOp_mul_coeff]

/-- Rescaling the coefficients `cᵢ` by constants `κᵢ` rescales `S(w, -)` by `∏ₐ κ_{w_a}`. -/
theorem vermaForm_mul_coeff (c : X → (X →₀ ℕ) → R) (κ : X → R) (w : List X)
    (y : FreeAlgebra R X) :
    vermaForm (fun i μ ↦ κ i * c i μ) w y = (w.map κ).prod * vermaForm c w y := by
  induction w generalizing y with
  | nil => simp
  | cons i w ih =>
    rw [vermaForm_cons, vermaOp_mul_coeff, LinearMap.smul_apply, map_smul, ih, vermaForm_cons,
      List.map_cons, List.prod_cons, smul_eq_mul]
    ring

end LusztigF

namespace Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping

variable {ι K H : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Field K] [AddCommGroup H] [Module K H]
  {A : Matrix ι ι ℤ} {P : Realization A K H} {p : ι → ZMod 2} [CharZero K]

/-- The enveloping superalgebra `U(G̃(A, τ))`. -/
local notation "𝒰" => SuperEnveloping P p

variable (K A) in
/-- The super Verma coefficients `cᵢ(μ) = nᵢ - ⟨μ, αᵢ^∨⟩`. -/
def superVermaCoeff (n : ι → ℕ) (i : ι) (μ : ι →₀ ℕ) : K :=
  ((n i : ℤ) - (A *ᵥ natVec μ) i : ℤ)

/-! ### Weight vectors generated by vectors killed by the `eᵢ` -/

section Span

variable {V : Type*} [AddCommGroup V] [Module K V] [Module (P.SuperEnveloping p) V]
  [IsScalarTower K (P.SuperEnveloping p) V]

/-- A nonzero weight vector `v` in the submodule generated by a vector `g` of weight `μ` killed by
the `eᵢ` has weight in `μ - Q₊`. -/
lemma exists_eq_sub_of_mem_span_singleton (hV : IsGModule P p V) {μ ν : Dual K H} {g v : V}
    (hg : g ∈ modWeightSpace P p V μ) (he : ∀ j, e P p j • g = 0)
    (hv : v ∈ modWeightSpace P p V ν) (hv0 : v ≠ 0) (hmem : v ∈ Submodule.span 𝒰 {g}) :
    ∃ d : ι → ℤ, 0 ≤ d ∧ ν = μ - P.rootOf d := by
  let φ : GVerma P p μ →ₗ[𝒰] V :=
    GVerma.lift hV g he fun a ↦ by rw [algebraMap_smul]; exact hg a
  have hle : Submodule.span 𝒰 {g} ≤ LinearMap.range φ := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact ⟨GVerma.hwv P p μ, GVerma.lift_hwv _ _ _ _⟩
  have hB : IsBounded P p (LinearMap.range φ) {μ} :=
    GVerma.isBounded.of_surjective φ.rangeRestrict φ.surjective_rangeRestrict
  obtain ⟨μ', hμ', d, hd, hdeq⟩ := hB.exists_eq_sub (w := ⟨v, hle hmem⟩) (ν := ν)
    (fun a ↦ Subtype.ext (hv a)) (fun h ↦ hv0 (congr_arg Subtype.val h))
  exact ⟨d, hd, Finset.mem_singleton.1 hμ' ▸ hdeq⟩

/-- A nonzero weight vector `v` in the submodule generated by vectors `gᵢ` of weights `μᵢ` killed
by the `eⱼ` has weight in `μᵢ - Q₊` for some `i`. -/
lemma exists_eq_sub_of_mem_span_range (hV : IsGModule P p V) {μ : ι → Dual K H} {ν : Dual K H}
    (g : ι → V) (hg : ∀ i, g i ∈ modWeightSpace P p V (μ i)) (he : ∀ i j, e P p j • g i = 0)
    {v : V} (hv : v ∈ modWeightSpace P p V ν) (hv0 : v ≠ 0)
    (hmem : v ∈ Submodule.span 𝒰 (Set.range g)) :
    ∃ i, ∃ d : ι → ℤ, 0 ≤ d ∧ ν = μ i - P.rootOf d := by
  classical
  let φ (i : ι) : GVerma P p (μ i) →ₗ[𝒰] V :=
    GVerma.lift hV (g i) (he i) fun a ↦ by rw [algebraMap_smul]; exact hg i a
  let Φ : (∀ i, GVerma P p (μ i)) →ₗ[𝒰] V :=
    ∑ i, (φ i).comp (LinearMap.proj i)
  have hle : Submodule.span 𝒰 (Set.range g) ≤ LinearMap.range Φ := by
    refine Submodule.span_le.2 ?_
    rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨Pi.single i (GVerma.hwv P p (μ i)), ?_⟩
    simp only [Φ, LinearMap.sum_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.proj_apply]
    rw [Finset.sum_eq_single i (fun j _ hj ↦ by rw [Pi.single_eq_of_ne hj, map_zero])
      (by simp), Pi.single_eq_same, GVerma.lift_hwv]
  have hB : IsBounded P p (LinearMap.range Φ) (Finset.univ.biUnion fun i ↦ {μ i}) :=
    (isBounded_pi fun _ ↦ GVerma.isBounded).of_surjective Φ.rangeRestrict
      Φ.surjective_rangeRestrict
  obtain ⟨μ', hμ', d, hd, hdeq⟩ := hB.exists_eq_sub (w := ⟨v, hle hmem⟩) (ν := ν)
    (fun a ↦ Subtype.ext (hv a)) (fun h ↦ hv0 (congr_arg Subtype.val h))
  obtain ⟨i, -, hi⟩ := Finset.mem_biUnion.1 hμ'
  exact ⟨i, d, hd, Finset.mem_singleton.1 hi ▸ hdeq⟩

end Span

/-! ### The action of the `eᵢ` -/

namespace GVerma

variable {Λ : Dual K H} {n : ι → ℕ}

lemma fAlg_smul_hwv_mem {ν : ι →₀ ℕ} {t : FreeAlgebra K ι} (ht : t ∈ wordSpan K ν) :
    fAlg P p t • hwv P p Λ ∈
      modWeightSpace P p (GVerma P p Λ) (-P.rootOf (natVec ν) + Λ) :=
  smul_mem_modWeightSpace _ (fAlg_mem_weightSpace_of_mem_wordSpan P p ht)
    (hwv_mem_modWeightSpace (Λ := Λ))

/-- `eᵢ (f(y) v̄_Λ) = f(Eᵢ y) v̄_Λ` for the twisted Verma-type operator `Eᵢ` with signs
`(-1)^{τᵢτⱼ}` and coefficients `cᵢ(μ) = nᵢ - ⟨μ, αᵢ^∨⟩`. -/
theorem e_smul_fAlg_smul_hwv (hn : ∀ i, Λ (P.coroot i) = n i) (i : ι) (t : FreeAlgebra K ι) :
    e P p i • (fAlg P p t • hwv P p Λ) =
      fAlg P p (twistVermaOp i (superSign K p i) (superVermaCoeff K A n i) t) • hwv P p Λ := by
  induction t using induction_wordBasis with
  | zero => simp
  | add y z hy hz => rw [map_add, add_smul, smul_add, hy, hz, map_add, map_add, add_smul]
  | smul a y hy => rw [map_smul, smul_assoc, smul_comm, hy, map_smul, map_smul, smul_assoc]
  | word w =>
    induction w with
    | nil => simp [e_smul_hwv]
    | cons j w ih =>
      rw [← ι_mul_wordBasis, twistVermaOp_ι_mul, map_mul, fAlg_ι, mul_smul, ← mul_smul,
        e_mul_f, add_smul, smul_assoc, mul_smul, ih, map_add, map_smul, map_mul, fAlg_ι,
        add_smul, smul_assoc, mul_smul]
      congr 1
      split_ifs with hij
      · subst hij
        rw [weightScale_wordBasis, map_smul, smul_assoc,
          fAlg_smul_hwv_mem (wordBasis_mem_wordSpan w) (P.coroot i)]
        congr 1
        rw [LinearMap.add_apply, LinearMap.neg_apply, rootOf_apply_coroot, hn, superVermaCoeff]
        push_cast
        ring
      · simp

/-- If `f(y) v̄_Λ ∈ ∑ᵢ U fᵢ^{nᵢ+1} v̄_Λ` and `y` has weight `ν` with `νᵢ ≤ nᵢ` for all `i`, then
`f(y) v̄_Λ = 0`. -/
theorem fAlg_smul_hwv_eq_zero_of_mem_fPowSubmodule (hA : A.IsGeneralizedCartan)
    (hn : ∀ i, Λ (P.coroot i) = n i) (hodd : ∀ i, p i = 1 → Even (n i)) {ν : ι →₀ ℕ}
    (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≤ n i) {t : FreeAlgebra K ι} (ht : t ∈ wordSpan K ν)
    (hmem : fAlg P p t • hwv P p Λ ∈ fPowSubmodule P p Λ n) : fAlg P p t • hwv P p Λ = 0 := by
  by_contra h0
  obtain ⟨i, d, hd, hdeq⟩ := exists_eq_sub_of_mem_span_range (μ := fun i ↦ Λ - (n i + 1) • P.root i)
    isGModule _ (fun i ↦ f_pow_smul_mem_modWeightSpace hwv_mem_modWeightSpace i _)
    (fun i ↦ e_smul_f_pow_succ_smul_eq_zero hA (hn i) (hodd i) hwv_mem_modWeightSpace
      e_smul_hwv) (fAlg_smul_hwv_mem ht) h0 hmem
  have h0 : P.rootOf (d + ((n i + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) • Pi.single i 1 - natVec ν) = P.rootOf 0 := by
    rw [map_sub, map_add, map_zsmul, rootOf_single, map_zero, natCast_zsmul]
    linear_combination (norm := module) hdeq
  have h1 := congr_fun (P.rootOf_injective h0) i
  simp only [Pi.sub_apply, Pi.add_apply, Pi.smul_apply, Pi.single_eq_same, smul_eq_mul, mul_one,
    Pi.zero_apply, natVec] at h1
  have := hd i
  have := hν i
  simp only [Pi.zero_apply] at *
  omega

variable [FiniteDimensional K H] (S : A.Symmetrization) (hA : A.IsGeneralizedCartan)
  (hp : A.IsSuperAdmissible p)

include S hA hp in
/-- If all products of the `eᵢ` of weight `ν` kill `f(y) v̄_Λ` (in the form `S(w, y) = 0`), then
the image of `f(y) v̄_Λ` in the irreducible module `L̃(Λ)` is zero. -/
theorem mkQ_fAlg_smul_hwv_eq_zero (hn : ∀ i, Λ (P.coroot i) = n i)
    (hodd : ∀ i, p i = 1 → Even (n i)) (ν : ι →₀ ℕ) {t : FreeAlgebra K ι}
    (ht : t ∈ wordSpan K ν)
    (h : ∀ w, wordWeight w = ν →
      twistVermaForm (fun i ↦ superSign K p i) (superVermaCoeff K A n) w t = 0) :
    (fPowSubmodule P p Λ n).mkQ (fAlg P p t • hwv P p Λ) = 0 := by
  induction ν using WellFoundedLT.induction generalizing t with
  | ind ν ih =>
  set N := fPowSubmodule P p Λ n
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ : ∃ x, x = N.mkQ (fAlg P p t • hwv P p Λ) := ⟨_, rfl⟩
  rw [← hx]
  -- the `eᵢ` kill `x`
  have he : ∀ i, e P p i • x = 0 := fun i ↦ by
    rw [hx, ← map_smul, e_smul_fAlg_smul_hwv hn]
    by_cases hνi : ν i = 0
    · rw [twistVermaOp_eq_zero_of_mem i _ _ hνi ht, map_zero, zero_smul, map_zero]
    have hsi : Finsupp.single i 1 ≤ ν := Finsupp.single_le_iff.2 (Nat.one_le_iff_ne_zero.2 hνi)
    refine ih (ν - Finsupp.single i 1) (lt_of_le_of_ne tsub_le_self fun heq ↦ ?_)
      (twistVermaOp_mem_wordSpan i _ _ ht) fun w hw ↦ ?_
    · have := congr_arg (· i) heq
      simp only [Finsupp.coe_tsub, Pi.sub_apply, Finsupp.single_eq_same] at this
      omega
    · rw [← twistVermaForm_cons]
      exact h _ (by rw [wordWeight_cons, hw, add_tsub_cancel_of_le hsi])
  by_cases hν : ν = 0
  · subst hν
    have h0 := h [] rfl
    rw [twistVermaForm_apply, twistVermaWordOp_nil, Module.End.one_apply] at h0
    rw [hx, eq_algebraMap_of_mem_wordSpan_zero ht, h0, map_zero, map_zero, zero_smul, map_zero]
  by_contra hx0
  have := isSimpleModule_fPowQuotient S hA hp hn hodd
  have htop : Submodule.span 𝒰 {x} = ⊤ :=
    (IsSimpleOrder.eq_bot_or_eq_top _).resolve_left
      (by rwa [Submodule.span_singleton_eq_bot])
  have hv0 : N.mkQ (hwv P p Λ) ≠ 0 := fun h0 ↦ fPowSubmodule_ne_top hA hn hodd <| by
    rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at h0
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← span_hwv (P := P) (p := p) (Λ := Λ), Submodule.span_le,
      Set.singleton_subset_iff]
    exact h0
  have hxw : x ∈ modWeightSpace P p (FPowQuotient P p Λ n) (-P.rootOf (natVec ν) + Λ) :=
    fun a ↦ by rw [hx, ← map_smul, fAlg_smul_hwv_mem ht a, LinearMap.map_smul_of_tower]
  have hvw : N.mkQ (hwv P p Λ) ∈ modWeightSpace P p (FPowQuotient P p Λ n) Λ :=
    fun a ↦ by rw [← map_smul, hwv_mem_modWeightSpace a, LinearMap.map_smul_of_tower]
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hdeq⟩ := exists_eq_sub_of_mem_span_singleton isGModule_fPowQuotient hxw he hvw
    hv0 (htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top)
  have h0 : P.rootOf (natVec ν + d) = P.rootOf 0 := by
    rw [map_add, map_zero]
    linear_combination (norm := module) hdeq
  have h1 := P.rootOf_injective h0
  refine hν (Finsupp.ext fun i ↦ ?_)
  have := congr_fun h1 i
  have := hd i
  simp only [Pi.add_apply, natVec, Pi.zero_apply, Finsupp.coe_zero] at *
  omega

include S hA hp in
/-- **The kernel of the super Shapovalov pairing.** Let `⟨Λ, αᵢ^∨⟩ = nᵢ ∈ ℕ` with `nᵢ` even for
odd `τᵢ`. If `y ∈ T(V)` has weight `ν` with `νᵢ ≤ nᵢ` for all `i`, and the super Shapovalov
pairing `S(w, y)` vanishes for all words `w` of weight `ν`, then `y` lies in the ideal generated by
the super Serre elements. -/
theorem mem_superSerreIdeal_of_twistVermaForm_eq_zero (hn : ∀ i, Λ (P.coroot i) = n i)
    (hodd : ∀ i, p i = 1 → Even (n i)) {ν : ι →₀ ℕ} (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≤ n i)
    {t : FreeAlgebra K ι} (ht : t ∈ wordSpan K ν)
    (h : ∀ w, wordWeight w = ν →
      twistVermaForm (fun i ↦ superSign K p i) (superVermaCoeff K A n) w t = 0) :
    t ∈ superSerreIdeal K A p := by
  have h0 := mkQ_fAlg_smul_hwv_eq_zero S hA hp hn hodd ν ht h
  rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at h0
  exact (fAlg_smul_hwv_eq_zero_iff_mem_superSerreIdeal S hA hp Λ).1
    (fAlg_smul_hwv_eq_zero_of_mem_fPowSubmodule hA hn hodd hν ht h0)

end GVerma

end Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping

/-! ### Weight components of the super Serre ideal -/

namespace Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping

open FreeAlgebra

variable {ι K : Type*} [Field K] (A : Matrix ι ι ℤ) (p : ι → ZMod 2)

/-- The pairs `(i, j)` with `i ≠ j`, indexing the super Serre elements. -/
abbrev SerrePair (ι : Type*) := {ij : ι × ι // ij.1 ≠ ij.2}

variable (K) in
/-- The super Serre elements `sᵢⱼ`, `i ≠ j`, as a family. -/
def superSerreFamily (ij : SerrePair ι) : FreeAlgebra K ι :=
  superSerreFree K A p ij.1.1 ij.1.2

/-- The weight `αⱼ + (1 - aᵢⱼ) αᵢ` of `sᵢⱼ`. -/
def superSerreWeight (ij : SerrePair ι) : ι →₀ ℕ :=
  Finsupp.single ij.1.2 1 +
    LusztigF.wordWeight (List.replicate ((-A ij.1.1 ij.1.2).toNat + 1) ij.1.1)

lemma superSerreFamily_mem_wordSpan (ij : SerrePair ι) :
    superSerreFamily K A p ij ∈ wordSpan K (superSerreWeight A ij) :=
  sLie_mem_wordSpan (K := K) (p := p) ij.1.2 _

variable {A p}

/-- An element of weight `ν` lies in the super Serre ideal iff it is a combination of products
`a sᵢⱼ b` of weight `ν` with words `a`, `b`. -/
theorem mem_superSerreIdeal_iff_mem_productSpan {ν : ι →₀ ℕ} {y : FreeAlgebra K ι}
    (hy : y ∈ wordSpan K ν) :
    y ∈ superSerreIdeal K A p ↔
      y ∈ productSpan (superSerreFamily K A p) (superSerreWeight A) ν := by
  rw [← wordSpan_inf_ideal_eq_productSpan (superSerreFamily_mem_wordSpan A p) ν hy]
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine Submodule.span_induction (p := fun x _ ↦ x ∈ TwoSidedIdeal.span
      (Set.range (superSerreFamily K A p))) ?_ (zero_mem _) (fun _ _ _ _ ↦ add_mem)
      (fun a x _ hx ↦ TwoSidedIdeal.mul_mem_left _ a x hx) h
    rintro _ ⟨i, j, hij, b, rfl⟩
    exact TwoSidedIdeal.mul_mem_right _ _ _
      (TwoSidedIdeal.subset_span ⟨⟨(i, j), hij⟩, rfl⟩)
  · intro h
    clear hy
    induction h using TwoSidedIdeal.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
      obtain ⟨ij, rfl⟩ := hx
      simpa [superSerreFamily] using
        superSerreFree_mul_mem (K := K) (A := A) (p := p) ij.2 1
    | zero => exact zero_mem _
    | add x y _ _ hx hy => exact add_mem hx hy
    | neg x _ hx => exact neg_mem hx
    | left_absorb a x _ hx => exact Submodule.smul_mem _ a hx
    | right_absorb b x _ hx => exact mul_mem_superSerreIdeal hx b

end Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping

/-! ### The super kernel for a Cartan datum -/

namespace LusztigF

open Matrix.Realization Matrix.Realization.SuperEnveloping

variable {K I : Type*} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I] [Field K] [CharZero K]
  (D : LusztigCartanDatum I)

omit [DecidableEq I] [CharZero K] in
lemma superVermaCoeff_eq_classicalCoeff (n : I → ℕ) (i : I) (μ : I →₀ ℕ) :
    superVermaCoeff K D.cartanMatrix n i μ = classicalCoeff K D n i μ := by
  rw [superVermaCoeff, classicalCoeff, LusztigCartanDatum.coPairing,
    Finsupp.sum_fintype _ _ (by simp)]
  congr 3
  simp [Matrix.mulVec, dotProduct, natVec, mul_comm]

omit [Fintype I] in
/-- **The super kernel.** Let `p` be a super-admissible parity for the Cartan matrix of `D`, and
let the coefficients `c` differ from the classical ones of highest weight `n` (`nᵢ` even for odd
`i`) by the sign characters `μ ↦ ∏ₖ (-1)^{pᵢpₖμₖ}` and nonzero scalars `sᵢ`. If `y ∈ 'f_ν` with
`νᵢ ≤ nᵢ` pairs to zero with all words for the pairing `S_c`, then `y` lies in the ideal generated
by the super Serre elements. -/
theorem mem_superSerreIdeal_of_shapovalovMap_eq_zero [Finite I] {p : I → ZMod 2}
    (hp : D.cartanMatrix.IsSuperAdmissible p) (n : I → ℕ) (hodd : ∀ i, p i = 1 → Even (n i))
    {c : I → (I →₀ ℕ) → K} {s : I → K} (hs : ∀ i, s i ≠ 0)
    (hc : ∀ i μ, c i μ = s i * (weightSign (superSign K p i) μ * classicalCoeff K D n i μ))
    {ν : I →₀ ℕ} (hν : ∀ i, ν i ≤ n i) {y : LusztigF K I} (hy : y ∈ weightSpace K ν)
    (h0 : shapovalovMap c ν y = 0) :
    y ∈ superSerreIdeal K D.cartanMatrix p := by
  have := Fintype.ofFinite I
  obtain ⟨S⟩ := Matrix.isSymmetrizable_iff_nonempty_symmetrization.1
    D.isSymmetrizable_cartanMatrix
  refine GVerma.mem_superSerreIdeal_of_twistVermaForm_eq_zero
    (P := Matrix.Realization.std D.cartanMatrix K) (Λ := stdWeightOver D n) S
    D.isGeneralizedCartan_cartanMatrix hp (stdWeightOver_coroot D n) hodd hν hy fun w hw ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨u, -, hu⟩ := exists_twistVermaForm_eq_mul (fun i ↦ superSign K p i)
    (superSign_mul_self K p) (superVermaCoeff K D.cartanMatrix n) w ν
  rw [hu y hy]
  have h1 : vermaForm c w y = 0 := congr_fun h0 ⟨w, hw⟩
  have hc' : c = fun i μ ↦ s i * (weightSign (superSign K p i) μ *
      superVermaCoeff K D.cartanMatrix n i μ) := by
    funext i μ; rw [hc, superVermaCoeff_eq_classicalCoeff]
  rw [hc', vermaForm_mul_coeff] at h1
  have hprod : (w.map s).prod ≠ 0 := List.prod_ne_zero (by simpa using fun i _ ↦ hs i)
  rw [(mul_eq_zero.1 h1).resolve_left hprod, mul_zero]

end LusztigF
